# Postman documentation standard

Whenever creating or updating Postman requests (MCP or local `postman/*.json`), **never** ship one-line descriptions. Match **Gazebo - Food API** style (see List suppliers / Save product flags).

## Every request description must include

1. Title heading: `### <Action name>`
2. Route line: `` `METHOD /path/:param/` ``
3. Short purpose paragraph (what / why, real example when useful)
4. **Path parameters** table (if any)
5. **Query parameters** table (if any) — mark required/optional
6. **Request body** — `**None**.` or field table (required?, meaning)
7. **Response body** — shape, important fields, success message text
8. **Status codes** table (200/201/400/404/409 as applicable)

## Folder description

When adding a folder, set a markdown overview: domain purpose, table name, key vars.

## Do not

- One-liners like "GET list" or "POST create"
- Skip status codes or field tables on write endpoints
